---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../../utils/paths.js';

let currentVersion = '0.4.1';
try {
  const versionPath = path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, '../../../../VERSION');
  if (fs.existsSync(versionPath)) {
    currentVersion = fs.readFileSync(versionPath, 'utf8').replace(/#.*/g, '').trim();
  }
} catch {
  // fallback
}
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Changelog"
  description="What changed in each JobFoundry release, from the 0.1.0 beginnings to the current packaged distribution."
  currentPath={resolvePath('/docs/changelog/')}
  category="Project"
>
  <h1>Changelog</h1>
  <p>
    JobFoundry follows <a href="https://semver.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Semantic Versioning</a>.
    The current release is <strong>v{currentVersion}</strong>.
    For the complete release history, automated changelogs, and binary downloads, see
    <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>GitHub Releases</strong></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>0.5.1 — 2026-10-05</h2>
  <p>Container automation and packaging maintenance.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Automated GHCR container publishing on release and updated container workflows.</li>
    <li>Repaired Python packaging dependencies and synchronized VERSION metadata.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>0.5.0 — 2026-10-05</h2>
  <p>Tailoring engine upgrades, quick actions, and UX enhancements.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Tailoring Engine:</strong> Custom tailoring instructions, sequential cascade re-ranking, and post-tailor critic checks.</li>
    <li><strong>Web Dashboard:</strong> One-click "Mark Applied" directly on feed cards, elevated resume export toolbar, and rich provenance tracking.</li>
    <li><strong>Community Support:</strong> Built-in support modal with direct links to GitHub Sponsors and project contributions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>0.4.1 — 2026-09-30</h2>
  <p>macOS Apple Silicon distribution and documentation overhaul.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS Apple Silicon tarball</strong> (darwin-arm64) and official Homebrew formula.</li>
    <li>Comprehensive project docs: Architecture, Manifesto, Governance, Support, and contributor guides.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>0.4.0 — 2026-09-12</h2>
  <p>First packaged distribution release.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Windows 11 MSIX sideload package</strong> with Start-menu launch and control CLI.</li>
    <li><strong>Linux AppImage</strong>: single portable file, no Docker required.</li>
    <li>Dashboard unification: settings categories, onboarding quickstart, triage station.</li>
    <li>Per-user LLM settings (multi-tenant BYOK) and multi-model catalog.</li>
    <li>SSRF + credential-leak guard on the LLM API base URL.</li>
    <li>Runtime baseline: Node 26.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>0.3.0 — 2026-09-02</h2>
  <p>The "everything local" consolidation.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>resume-ops merged into <code>server/tailor</code></strong> — the standalone tailoring service became the integrated engine.</li>
    <li>Single All-in-One container on GHCR; one-command installer.</li>
    <li>Extension dashboard, side panel, secure auto-connect; background worker daemon.</li>
    <li>Docs portal, contributor and security guides.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>0.2.x — June–July 2026</h2>
  <p>Tailoring quality and configurability: ATS plaintext output, configurable retries and caching, folio as the default PDF theme with runtime theme loading.</p>

  <h2>0.1.x — June 2026</h2>
  <p>Initial history: monorepo scaffold (AGPL-3.0), ingest API with SQLite + SimHash dedup, LangGraph tailoring pipeline, GHCR publishing.</p>
</DocsLayout>
